# What is deliberately not in this repository, and why.
#
# The rule: source and recipes are tracked, anything a recipe produces is not, and
# anything belonging to someone else is not. That keeps the tree small enough to
# clone and keeps third-party material out of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------- other people's code

# The extracted S60 3rd Edition FP2 SDK: ~1 GB of Nokia's headers, import libraries
# and tools. Proprietary, and not ours to redistribute. Rebuild it with
# vendor/gnupoc-git and the original Nokia installer; tools/symbuild takes its
# location from EPOCROOT in app.conf, so it does not have to live here.
/sdk/

# Third-party sources and preserved research artifacts: GnuPoc, the Telegram TL
# schema, S60 documentation, theme files, irssi sources. Mixed licences, ~800 MB.
# Our own change to elf2e32 is tracked as a patch under toolchain/patches/ instead,
# which is the part worth keeping under review.
/vendor/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ build products

# The cross toolchain: 1.6 GB of built GCC and binutils, plus their source trees.
# toolchain/build-cross-gcc.sh and toolchain/patches/ are the recipe and are
# tracked; everything the recipe produces is not.
/toolchain/cross/
/toolchain/src/
/toolchain/host/
/toolchain/*.log

# Cargo. The device crates are their own workspace roots (a #[panic_handler] cannot
# be built for the host), so each has a target/ of its own.
/target/
**/device/target/

# Per-app build directories: objects, ELF, E32, resources, .sis.
**/build/

# Staged packages, ready to push to a phone.
/out/

# Rendered UI previews. Regenerate with `cargo run -p preview`.
/preview-out/

# Generated icon bitmaps. The generator (data/mkicon.py) is the source; a checked-in
# .bmp is a binary nobody can review.
**/data/*_icon.bmp
**/data/*_icon_mask.bmp

# Generated resource headers, emitted by rcomp next to the .rss that includes them.
**/data/*.rsg

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets

# Self-signed development certificates, minted on demand by tools/symbuild when
# SIGN=1. Never useful to anyone else, and a private key in a repository is a
# private key on the internet.
/keys/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ credentials

# Every app's api.conf, wherever it sits. `tools/symbuild` sources this file if it is there
# and passes what it finds to the build: application credentials for whatever service the app
# talks to, and EPOCADB_HOST, which is one machine's LAN address and nobody else's build
# setting. An app tracks `api.conf.example` instead, saying what belongs in it.
#
# Matched by name rather than by path, because an app is a directory that can move — and did.
# An app in its own repository should carry this same rule in its own .gitignore, since this
# one stops applying the moment it leaves.
api.conf
**/api.conf

# Agent worktrees: transient checkouts, not source.
/.claude/worktrees/
